WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.200
I'm not sure I agree with that.

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:01.520
OK.

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:02.880
I think if you're democratically amending

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:04.560
the Constitution per the rules of the Constitution,

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:05.240
that's fine.

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:06.680
If we could find a constitutional way

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:08.820
to get rid of the Second Amendment, I'd be pro that.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.540
So let's pose a hypothetical wherein

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:13.240
the entire population of the United States

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:14.440
has drastically changed.

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:14.940
Yes.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.780
And the population now has completely different intentions

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.160
about what to do with the country.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.240
Let's say it wants to give it all back to Mexico,

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.440
dismantling the United States of America.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.840
If that's the case, then what's the use of the Constitution?

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:28.120
It hasn't defended the country.

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:30.400
In fact, it's allowed for its destruction.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:31.320
I don't understand the premise.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.919
How did the whole country change?

00:00:32.919 --> 00:00:34.040
Demographic replacement.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:34.900
Mass migration.

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:37.520
I mean, we're seeing a change in demographics.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:38.680
And there's-

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:40.160
What is the-

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:41.959
I do want to talk about immigration today.

00:00:41.959 --> 00:00:42.599
I hope we talk about it.

00:00:42.599 --> 00:00:44.799
Everyone's itching in this group to get to immigration.

00:00:44.799 --> 00:00:45.200
Yes, sir.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:45.759
I've saved it.

00:00:45.759 --> 00:00:46.840
I've saved it for you all.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:48.840
But given we're on the sense of the Constitution,

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:50.880
and you asked a question, what is the proportion

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:52.560
of immigrants in this country?

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:54.680
What proportion of the population is foreign born?

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:57.799
It's very difficult to measure, because the actual projections

00:00:57.799 --> 00:00:59.720
of the number have been changing more rapidly.

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:02.279
But what is currently the best estimate of official-

00:01:02.279 --> 00:01:03.480
I think it was about 15%.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:04.000
Yes.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.080
Just under 15%.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:07.040
Which is, by the way, which is more, actually,

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:08.760
than the original estimate was.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:11.199
But 15% of the people are going to change the country,

00:01:11.199 --> 00:01:11.919
change the Constitution.

00:01:11.919 --> 00:01:12.720
How's that going to make sense?

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:13.480
It's actually a nightmare.

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:15.400
As someone who wants to amend the Constitution

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.559
and get rid of things like the ridiculous way

00:01:17.559 --> 00:01:19.839
the Senate is set up, or the Second Amendment on guns,

00:01:19.839 --> 00:01:21.919
or various other things, it's really hard

00:01:21.919 --> 00:01:23.040
to change the Constitution.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.480
They made it almost impossible.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:25.879
You know the last time we had a Constitutional Amendment?

00:01:25.879 --> 00:01:26.160
You know what?

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:27.080
Like 20, 30 years ago.

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:27.559
I understand.

00:01:27.559 --> 00:01:29.279
And it was all, I think, members of Congress paying.

00:01:29.279 --> 00:01:29.760
Which is why-

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:30.400
It's impossible.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:30.919
No, I get it.

00:01:30.919 --> 00:01:33.160
So where are you getting this scenario where

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:36.239
350-odd million people all become foreign-born migrants,

00:01:36.239 --> 00:01:38.279
or the children of migrants, immediate migrants,

00:01:38.279 --> 00:01:40.120
even though America is a nation of migrants,

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:41.919
and then abandon the Constitution

00:01:41.919 --> 00:01:43.440
and give the country back to Mexico?

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.959
Outside of your imagination, where is that happening?

00:01:45.959 --> 00:01:48.040
Well, let's bring it back to the actual discussion.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:50.599
What you did is you entertained my hypothetical.

00:01:50.599 --> 00:01:53.199
But then instead of sticking to the point of the Constitution,

00:01:53.199 --> 00:01:55.040
you said, well, how would you bring about your hypothetical?

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:55.480
And then when I gave you-

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:57.120
Because you missed out the part where the Constitution's

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:57.919
quite hard to change.

00:01:57.919 --> 00:01:57.959
Hold on.

00:01:57.959 --> 00:01:58.480
Hold on.

00:01:58.480 --> 00:01:59.559
I understand that.

00:01:59.559 --> 00:02:00.040
I gave you a simple-

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:01.519
I also wanted to get a sense of where you are,

00:02:01.519 --> 00:02:03.480
and you're a great replacement guy, so that's fine.

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:04.000
OK.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.239
Yeah, and you're a real good journalist

00:02:05.239 --> 00:02:06.800
because you don't talk to people who identify

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:08.199
as like a political ideology.

00:02:08.199 --> 00:02:09.800
I mean, that's a very literal idea.

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:10.839
No, I don't debate fascists.

00:02:10.839 --> 00:02:12.240
I'll talk to them, but I wouldn't debate them.

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:13.479
Frankly, that's upsetting.

00:02:13.479 --> 00:02:14.960
I think there's a big problem when, you know,

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:16.360
we value freedom of speech so much,

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:18.800
but any real journalist is not going to talk to somebody

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:21.039
because they identify with a politically incorrect ideology.

00:02:21.039 --> 00:02:22.399
Just talk to the guy in front of you.

00:02:22.399 --> 00:02:22.960
What are you talking about?

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:24.639
You literally stop talking to him,

00:02:24.679 --> 00:02:25.880
and then everybody has to vote him out.

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:27.919
Debating versus talking is very different.

00:02:27.919 --> 00:02:28.759
It's pointless, right?

00:02:28.759 --> 00:02:30.559
He doesn't believe in free speech.

00:02:30.559 --> 00:02:30.960
OK.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:32.039
He doesn't believe in democracy.

00:02:32.039 --> 00:02:33.000
He was freely speaking with you.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:33.880
You're the one who shut up.

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:35.039
No, he said it very clearly.

00:02:35.039 --> 00:02:37.919
OK, so I support free speech so that I can get one election.

00:02:37.919 --> 00:02:40.080
After one election, my guy comes in,

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:43.240
and after my guy comes in, nobody gets to speak or vote again.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:44.199
Why would I debate that?

00:02:44.199 --> 00:02:45.119
We listened to your conversation.

00:02:45.119 --> 00:02:46.399
Well, I'm reminding you what it was said,

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:47.559
because you just misrepresented it.

00:02:47.559 --> 00:02:48.279
Let's bring it back to the Constitution.

00:02:48.279 --> 00:02:48.880
Please do.

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:51.880
First, fourth, fifth, 14th amendments.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:53.279
Those are the ones I'm saying Trump is defying.

00:02:53.279 --> 00:02:54.919
Do you support that, or do you deny them?

00:02:54.919 --> 00:02:56.720
I believe that the Constitution is valuable

00:02:56.720 --> 00:02:59.559
because it represents particular interests of the founding

00:02:59.559 --> 00:03:01.160
stock of Americans who made this country great.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:02.559
Do you think due process is important?

00:03:02.559 --> 00:03:04.479
Some would say that's at the very core of American

00:03:04.479 --> 00:03:05.759
Constitution, Fifth Amendment.

00:03:05.759 --> 00:03:08.559
And what I think makes the Constitution function,

00:03:08.559 --> 00:03:11.080
what allows it to save this country

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:13.559
and to actually make it work, are the people who are.

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:15.679
I'm not sure where you're going with this argument.

00:03:15.679 --> 00:03:17.279
Is Trump defying the Constitution?

00:03:17.279 --> 00:03:18.199
That's my claim.

00:03:18.199 --> 00:03:19.800
You can have these weird hypotheticals about it.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:21.919
We're taking it into a different meta, which is,

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:23.240
what's the function of the Constitution?

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:24.240
I'd rather not have your-

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:24.919
You already did.

00:03:24.919 --> 00:03:26.559
You already did, literally just five minutes ago

00:03:26.559 --> 00:03:27.960
when you took it to immigration, pal.

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:29.240
Okay, let's bring it back.

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:31.399
I want to bring it back to the first, the fourth,

00:03:31.399 --> 00:03:32.839
the fifth, and the 14th amendments,

00:03:32.839 --> 00:03:34.119
and the 22nd amendments.

00:03:34.119 --> 00:03:35.559
Then let me throw it to your question.

00:03:35.559 --> 00:03:36.919
You've got two very good positions here.

00:03:36.919 --> 00:03:38.839
One is to say, I don't think he's defying them,

00:03:38.839 --> 00:03:40.119
and I'll say why you're wrong.

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:41.919
Or you say, I don't care that he's defying them,

00:03:41.919 --> 00:03:44.320
as one of your colleagues said, in which case,

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:45.440
I don't know where this conversation goes

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:46.679
because you don't believe in democracy.

00:03:46.679 --> 00:03:47.919
That's fair.

00:03:47.919 --> 00:03:49.839
Do you think it's wrong to dismantle the Constitution?

